 # Captain Notes
 
-## Voyage 2: Browser-page delivery
+## Voyage 3: Row identity and edit-mode controls
 
-Intent: The app must render and run as a real web page in a browser.
-Currently: no `index.html` at the project root. The template at `assets/app-template.index.html` is only consumed by the happy-dom test harness. The app behaviour is fully proven (34 passing scenarios) but unreachable from a browser.
+Intent: Fix two defects in the todo app — row element identity lost on toggle, and controls visible during editing.
 
-Authored:
-- `features/app-page.feature` — 6 new scenarios covering file existence, markup structure, JS loading, and interactive rendering.
-- `watchbill.json` — watch1 orders the 6 new scenarios for QM.
+### Defect 1 — Row identity on toggle
+`render()` rebuilds `todoList.innerHTML` from scratch on every state change, destroying and recreating every `<li>`. A reference to a toggled row becomes stale immediately after the click.
 
-Status: working tree clean at base, specs and watchbill written, ready for QM dispatch.
+Fix: Change `render()` to update existing rows in place — reuse each todo's `<li>`, keyed by the todo, creating/removing only rows that were added/removed. A toggle mutates the row already on the page instead of rebuilding the list.
 
-## Decisions
-- `index.html` will be built from `assets/app-template.index.html`, the template the specs reference.
-- The template's CSS links (`node_modules/todomvc-common/base.css`, `node_modules/todomvc-app-css/index.css`) and the `base.js` script reference will be included per the template structure. The `todomvc-common` and `todomvc-app-css` packages are not installed — that is a production concern for Crew.
-- No existing feature files or step definitions were modified. All existing behaviour preserved.
-- RIGGING.md has no `conformance` command slot; no methodology checks were derived for this voyage. The first harbour will fit them.
\ No newline at end of file
+Discriminating scenario: `features/todo-item.feature` — three new scenarios under Rule "Toggle preserves the list element identity" that capture a reference to a specific `<li>`, toggle, and assert the same element object still carries the updated state.
+
+### Defect 2 — Controls hidden during edit
+When a row is in edit mode (`li.editing`), the `.view` div (checkbox, label, destroy button) remains visible. The app needs a CSS rule at `css/app.css` that hides `.view` inside `li.editing`, so the controls are not visible regardless of where the app is served.
+
+Fix: Add to `css/app.css`: a rule targeting `.view` within `li.editing` to `display: none`.
+
+Discriminating scenario: `features/todo-editing.feature` — one new scenario under Rule "Editing mode hides other controls" that asserts the checkbox, label, and destroy button are not visible when the row is in edit mode.
+
+### Specs authored
+- `features/todo-item.feature` — added 3 scenarios under new Rule "Toggle preserves the list element identity"
+- `features/todo-editing.feature` — added 1 scenario under new Rule "Editing mode hides other controls"
+- `watchbill.json` — created with watch1 ordering the 4 new scenarios
+
+### Decisions
+- All 40 existing scenarios pass and are unmodified. All existing behaviour preserved.
+- The two fixes are independent: row-identity fix in `js/app.js`, and edit-mode CSS rule in `css/app.css`.
+- `css/app.css` does not exist yet. It must be created with the editing-controls rule and loaded by `index.html` (the link already exists in the template).
+
+Status: specs written, watchbill set, working tree clean. Ready for QM dispatch.
\ No newline at end of file
